    "contentHtml": "<h2>Module Capabilities</h2><ul><li><strong>First Sign-In</strong>: Obtain an account and initial password from the supplier, project owner, or administrator; self-registration is not required. If prompted, change the initial password, then confirm that the expected modules and cameras are available.</li><li><strong>Daily Access</strong>: Sign in with your assigned username and password. The platform loads menus, camera resources, and actions according to the account’s role, so available content can differ by responsibility.</li><li><strong>Saved Credentials</strong>: Use <strong>Remember Me</strong> only on a trusted device under your control. Do not save credentials on a shared or public workstation.</li><li><strong>Account and Access Maintenance</strong>: Authorized administrators can create or edit users in Account Settings, then configure roles, feature permissions, and camera-resource scope in User Role Settings.</li><li><strong>Password Recovery</strong>: Select <strong>Forgot Password</strong> on the login page and use the email address bound to the account to receive a verification code or reset link. Sign in with the new password after verification; the account’s role and resource scope are unchanged.</li></ul><h2>Quick Guide</h2><ul><li><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://polytron-doc.vercel.app/en/docs/auth/login\">Login</a>: Sign in to POLYTRON ONE with the account assigned by your supplier or administrator. After authentication, the platform displays the pages, cameras, and actions allowed by the account’s role.</p></li><li><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://polytron-doc.vercel.app/en/docs/auth/forgot-password\">Forgot Password</a>: Recover access by verifying through the email address bound to your account and setting a new password. A password reset changes the sign-in credential, not the account’s role or camera permissions.</p></li></ul><h2>Recommended Workflow</h2><ol><li>Sign in with your assigned account and change the initial password if prompted.</li><li>Confirm that the expected menus and cameras are available. Ask an administrator to review the role and resource scope if anything is missing.</li><li>Have an authorized administrator use Account Settings and User Role Settings for new users or access changes.</li><li>Use the account’s bound email address to recover a forgotten password. Ask an administrator to check the account and mail service if verification fails or no email arrives.</li></ol>",
