    "contentHtml": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>System Logs records platform activity and key operations. For offline devices, missing footage, service errors, license expiry, memory or storage issues, or unusual account activity, start with the time of the issue and correlate the logs with the affected module.</p><p>Logs provide evidence for investigation. Fields and event coverage depend on the deployment; interpret each record alongside surrounding events and the actual operating state.</p><h2>Log Features</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Feature or Category</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>List and Details</th><td>Review dates, times, event types, and descriptions. Details may identify the object, outcome, failure reason, and related device or user.</td></tr><tr><th>Time and Keywords</th><td>Narrow the interval around an issue, then search by camera ID, username, device name, IP address, event type, or error text.</td></tr><tr><th>Filters</th><td>Use the log type, event type, outcome, or state criteria provided by the page.</td></tr><tr><th>Export</th><td>Export the filtered records for troubleshooting, archiving, reviews, or audits.</td></tr><tr><th>System Events</th><td>Inspect records related to licensing, services, storage, memory, restarts, and background tasks.</td></tr><tr><th>Device Connections</th><td>Review failures, offline events, recovery, reconnection, and restart-related state changes.</td></tr><tr><th>Recording Events</th><td>Check starts, stops, task changes, failures, and schedule errors when investigating missing footage.</td></tr><tr><th>User Activity and Sign-in</th><td>Review recorded sign-ins, sign-outs, results, and key changes to cameras, schedules, rules, permissions, or data exports.</td></tr><tr><th>Chronological Tracking</th><td>Follow a device, account, or service over time and correlate events around an error.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Investigation Scenarios</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Start with</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Preview Failure or Interrupted Stream</th><td>Connection failures, offline periods, reconnections, and recovery; correlate these with network and stream settings.</td></tr><tr><th>Missing Historical Footage</th><td>Recording starts, stops, and failures in the target interval; check schedules and storage.</td></tr><tr><th>Unexpected Configuration Changes</th><td>User operations and affected objects around the change time.</td></tr><tr><th>Unusual Sign-in Activity</th><td>Account, timestamp, and outcome; check account state and permissions.</td></tr><tr><th>Widespread or Platform Issues</th><td>Events affecting multiple cameras, tasks, or services at the same time; check system information and resources.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Investigation Procedure</h2><ol><li>Identify the issue time, camera or user, and visible error.</li><li>Narrow the time range, apply keyword and type filters, and review the sequence around the error.</li><li>Validate the findings in camera, recording, storage, or account settings. Export the relevant interval for recurring problems.</li><li>Retain the error text, affected objects, and checks already completed so another operator can continue the investigation.</li></ol><h2>Important Considerations</h2><p>Limit log viewing and export to the people responsible for those tasks. Exports may contain account, device, and configuration details; manage them according to the project’s access and retention requirements.</p><p>Set retention to cover investigation and audit needs. Short retention may remove needed history, while longer retention consumes more storage. Archive required records through the project’s process.</p><h2>Interface Example</h2><img src=\"/media/polytron-one/uploads/en/20260707013129-191ju9-active-log.png\" alt=\"active log\" title=\"active log\">",
