    "id": "en-getting-started-checklist",
    "title": "Getting Started Checklist",
    "route": "/en/docs/getting-started",
    "category": "System Overview",
    "status": "Published",
    "owner": "Product Operations",
    "updatedAt": "2026-11-03",
    "version": "1.4",
    "readingTime": 2,
    "summary": "Before monitoring begins, verify account access, live video, recordings, AI detection, and notification handling. Record any issues that need to be resolved.",
    "tags": [
      "Getting Started",
      "Checklist",
      "English"
    ],
    "contentHtml": "<h2>Before You Begin</h2><p>Obtain an account from the administrator and confirm that the workstation can access POLYTRON ONE. For the first check, work with an administrator or delivery specialist to identify a test camera, a recorded interval, the detection rule, and the required permissions.</p><p>Run detection tests only on approved devices and in an approved area under safe, controlled conditions. Coordinate the test so it does not disrupt monitoring or prompt an unnecessary site response.</p><h2>Acceptance Checklist</h2><ol><li>Sign-in and permissions: verify the menus, actions, and cameras required for the role.</li><li>Live video: open at least one authorized camera. Confirm that it plays, its displayed time is correct, and its device state is appropriate.</li><li>Recordings: select an interval known to contain footage and confirm that recording segments are visible and playable.</li><li>AI detection: under controlled conditions, perform an action that meets the test rule and check the detection and alarm record.</li><li>Notification response: open that alarm, review the clip, add a test note, and apply the agreed state action. Confirm that the list reflects the outcome.</li><li>Record the outcome: document passed checks and exceptions, including camera IDs, test times, errors, and screenshots, and assign follow-up to the responsible person.</li></ol><h2>Initial Use Guidance</h2><p>Before starting a shift, review camera availability, system resources, and outstanding alarms on Home, then prepare the usual grids or tabs in Live View. If significant issues remain, use the project’s acceptance and shift procedures to decide whether the system is ready for use.</p><p>Lock the workstation when stepping away and sign out when finished. Do not save credentials on a shared device.</p>",
