      {
        "id": "security-considerations",
        "heading": "Access and Sharing",
        "body": "Export only the cameras and time intervals needed for the task.Avoid unapproved personal cloud drives, messaging tools, or removable devices for transfers.Restrict recipients and storage locations according to project requirements when footage identifies people, work areas, or sensitive facilities.Before external sharing, confirm requirements for approval, redaction, watermarking, or encrypted transfer. These are handling requirements and do not imply that every processing tool is built into the platform."
      },
      {
        "id": "section-5",
        "heading": "Troubleshoot an Export",
        "body": "Verify that the source recording exists and plays, the trim interval is valid, downloads are permitted, and the local disk has space. For larger exports, shorten the interval or split it into clips. Check task and download states before submitting another request.Supported formats, maximum duration, and file-size limits depend on the deployment. If a file will not open, confirm that the download completed, try the project-recommended player, and retain the error, file size, and export interval for investigation."
      }
