    "contentHtml": "<h2>Accounts and Permissions</h2><h3>Why are some pages or cameras missing after sign-in?</h3><p>Check both feature permissions and camera-resource permissions for the assigned role. Access to a page does not necessarily include the required cameras. Ask the administrator to verify the access needed for your role.</p><h3>What if the password-reset email does not arrive?</h3><p>Use the email address bound to the account, check the spam folder, and use the latest code or link. If the email still does not arrive, ask the administrator to verify the address and mail service.</p><h2>Cameras and Live Video</h2><h3>Why is there no image when a camera is online?</h3><p>Online status describes basic connectivity. Check the stream URL, codec, browser media support, and account permissions, then test actual playback.</p><h3>Why can video quality decrease in a multi-camera view?</h3><p>Multi-camera views may use a lower-bitrate substream to reduce bandwidth and client load. Switch to a single view or an available higher-quality stream for detail. Supported modes depend on the device and deployment.</p><h2>Recordings and Exports</h2><h3>Why is no recording available in Playback?</h3><p>Verify the camera, date, time, and time zone, then check schedule coverage, storage, and recording-task execution. A camera being online now does not establish that footage exists for the interval.</p><h3>What if an exported video will not open?</h3><p>Confirm that the download completed and the file size is plausible, then try the project-recommended player. If it still fails, export a shorter interval and retain the error, footage interval, and camera ID.</p><h2>AI Alarms and Notifications</h2><h3>Why is no alarm triggered even though live video works?</h3><p>Check algorithm enablement, rule deployment, region, direction, threshold, duration, and active schedule. Validate with an approved, safe example that meets the rule.</p><h3>Why is a known alarm missing from Notifications?</h3><p>Check time and status filters, auto refresh, account visibility, and whether the event was closed or archived. Reading a notification or stopping an alert is separate from completing the response.</p><h3>How should I reduce frequent false alarms?</h3><p>Retain representative clips and document the causes. Inspect region size, reflections, background motion, occlusion, thresholds, and active periods. Adjust one relevant condition at a time and retest.</p><h2>Get Help</h2><p>Start with Troubleshooting. If the issue persists, provide the administrator with the page URL, time and time zone, camera ID, steps, expected and actual results, error text, screenshots, and relevant logs. Remove passwords, tokens, and complete credentials before sharing.</p>",
